From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:25:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] renderer: only disable blending when the main surface is
 the solitary one

CWindow::opaque() is also true when a single opaque subsurface covers
the window. drawSurface() used it to draw the *main* surface without
blending, but the subsurface's opacity says nothing about the main
surface's pixels. With GTK graphics offload the main surface is
transparent where a subsurface placed below it shows through. Drawn
without blending, that hole is written as black over the subsurface.

With rounding > 0 blending stays on, so this only shows with
decoration:rounding = 0, and on fullscreen windows. Epiphany with a
single tab rendered an all-black page on a tiled, unrounded window.

Keep opaque() for occlusion and blur decisions, and only skip blending
when the main surface is itself the solitary resource.
---
 src/render/ElementRenderer.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/render/ElementRenderer.cpp b/src/render/ElementRenderer.cpp
index 50b5a797..21c23ecf 100644
--- a/src/render/ElementRenderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/ElementRenderer.cpp
@@ -292,7 +292,13 @@ void IElementRenderer::drawSurface(WP<CSurfacePassElement> element, const CRegio
         roundingPower = 2.0f;
     }
 
-    const bool WINDOWOPAQUE    = m_data.pWindow && m_data.pWindow->wlSurface()->resource() == m_data.surface ? m_data.pWindow->opaque() : false;
+    // CWindow::opaque() describes the window as a whole, and it is also true when a single opaque
+    // subsurface covers the window (getSolitaryResource()). That says nothing about the main
+    // surface's own pixels: with GTK graphics offload the main surface is transparent where a
+    // subsurface placed *below* it shows through, and drawing it without blending paints that hole
+    // black. Only skip blending when the main surface itself is the solitary resource.
+    const bool MAINSURFACE     = m_data.pWindow && m_data.pWindow->wlSurface()->resource() == m_data.surface;
+    const bool WINDOWOPAQUE    = MAINSURFACE && m_data.pWindow->opaque() && m_data.pWindow->getSolitaryResource() == m_data.surface;
     const bool CANDISABLEBLEND = ALPHA >= 1.f && OVERALL_ALPHA >= 1.f && rounding <= 0 && WINDOWOPAQUE;
 
     if (CANDISABLEBLEND)
